# Kconfig fragment for the CVE-2024-1086 / nf_tables reproducer.
#
# Applied on top of the kernel's own `x86_64_defconfig` by
# `configs/generate-config.sh` (via `scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh`).
# Keeping only the options that matter here — instead of hand-editing and
# tracking a full 5000+ line `.config` — makes the security-relevant intent
# auditable and reproducible from a clean clone.
#
# Requirements (see README.md "Configuration requirements"): enable nf_tables
# and its netlink interface, user and network namespaces, and leave heap-init
# hardening disabled. NFNETLINK is the interface name; there is no
# CONFIG_NFNETLINK Kconfig symbol.
#
# User namespaces must also be permitted at runtime (kernel.unprivileged_userns_clone=1
# where that sysctl exists). On kernels newer than v6.4, heap-init hardening
# defeats the UAF/double-free the PoC relies on.

CONFIG_NF_TABLES=y
CONFIG_NETFILTER_NETLINK=y
CONFIG_USER_NS=y
CONFIG_NET_NS=y
# CONFIG_INIT_ON_ALLOC_DEFAULT_ON is not set
